    {
      "id": "p0118-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This same relationship issue appeared elsewhere during Underta/e's Japanese localization. For example, a store owner mentions that she has a sister who manages the inn. In English, these two are simply referred to as sisters, but the Japanese language only has words for \"younger sister\" or \"older sister\".",
        "raw": "This same relationship issue appeared elsewhere during Underta/e's Japanese\nlocalization. For example, a store owner mentions that she has a sister who\nmanages the inn. In English, these two are simply referred to as sisters, but the\nJapanese language only has words for \"younger sister\" or \"older sister\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29414053,
          0.62131429,
          0.90026005,
          0.68967143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29097696,
          0.6206,
          0.90706682,
          0.69074286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          41,
          42,
          43,
          44
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Undertale 的日语本地化中，其他地方也遇到了相同的亲属关系问题。例如，一位店主提到，她的姐妹经营着旅馆。英语只说明两人是姐妹，但日语需要区分“妹妹”或“姐姐”。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
